 "reviewer_manifest_sha256": "f2b3b666fb4d5d876b605307d56dd0a59ba02d690f7ec1190ba58f21cd04f8b4",
 "report": "23 serial cold launches of the prebuilt ELF matrix d17ce2d36c7c9bc4db40dc60fccec4f0ebfc8d29; all reached CONTROL END. Source clean at post-run HEAD. QEMU 6.2.0, single Cortex-A72, virt GICv2/TCG/128 MiB. Each case has argv, UART, stderr, exception trace. The first run rm-healthy failed initial IRQ lateness, raw SHA256 a43d63628e3f1b1d855ab9676c0dabafbc6712f3cf144e67236c94d2bc7b843f. All eight default-clock cases fail-inhibited before enabling. Neither negative demand nor late isolates the intended cause because both already showed the startup failure. The first RM loss skipped slot zero entirely. Code remains unmodified; do not treat these host-clock observations as intrinsic impossibility or admission.\n\nBoth policies with exact deterministic injector enable/handoff separately achieved measured healthy and loss behavior. First issue 190079, second 815079, command 1127579, enabled readback 1252634, transfer generation 1 sequence 3 at 1252637. Device readback is an in-guest volatile PL061 register read with ordered trace, not an external electrical observation. Observer measured falling transition at 3440132. limits.txt gives bracketing and exact threshold self-tests. No general analytical or hardware timing bound established. Exception traces show exception transfers; no continuous PRIMASK/DAIF measurement inferred.\n\nTwo deterministic RM script exact-boundary cases remain unqualified. Worst completed at 2658830 instead of 2658828, next gap 312503 instead of 312500. Tie issue followed expiry decision by six ticks. Inspect actual transaction and completion placement before requalification. The other nine scripts reproduced their state transitions; semantic reject/saturation checks are bounded stimulus, not a real transport. See summary.json, check.py and checker.txt. No default-clock handoff run was commissioned in this first matrix.\n",
